(text "CA02P-5 is ONBOARD, not an external supply. Nonisolated grounds 3/8; case 5 grounded.\nHold VPGM=0 for >=100 ms after module power, then ramp. Inhibit/removal of input\nand independent bleeders must be implemented on this sheet. Monitor raw HV AND FCOM.\nNominal 200 V module becomes about 199.6 V after 20k filter/9.98M bleeder; no 300 V claim." (at 20.32 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0adc89f7-1264-5e3b-adba-1ac509c2cec0"))
(text "1 DEFAULT OFF\nHV_ENABLE low: U22 removes module 5 V. Fault latches off.\nEither control low: 2N7002 clamps filtered command to 0 V.\nQ203/Q204 require PGM_RELEASE AND actual supply-ready." (at 15.24 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top)) (uuid "47e29dbe-e55c-56b7-944d-3981dbb8737d"))
(text "2 SEQUENCED ENABLE\nApply module power with command held zero. U23 holds reset 180-420 ms after actual module supply rises.\nRaise PGM_RELEASE; 10k / 47uF gives 0.47-0.588 s nominal ramp including pot resistance.\nAccept C210 only with effective C >=22uF at 2.048 V / temperature; measure settling.\nDisable by releasing command first, then removing module power." (at 162.56 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a615395b-7df0-58cb-8bdf-1a7511476e67"))
(text "Buffer remains powered from BUCK5. The input clamp drives a zero\nprogramming voltage while module power is off. 0-2.048 V programs 0-200 V; calibrate actual bias.\nHost controls are functional sequencing, not a certified beam interlock." (at 215.9 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a4636671-434d-5d99-8d39-384e23d73c9c"))
(embedded_fonts no)
)
